title: "statement-store: fix unbounded growth of the evicted-hashes map"
doc:
  - audience: Node Dev
    description: |
      The statement store keeps a map of recently-removed statement hashes to
      suppress re-gossip. This map could grow unboundedly over time.

      - Naturally-expired statements are no longer added to the evicted map.
        Re-gossip suppression is still guaranteed because `submit` rejects
        them unconditionally via `AlreadyExpired`.

      - The evicted map is now bounded to `max_total_statements` entries and
        uses deadline-ordered purging so maintenance is efficient.

      - The purge deadline for a forcibly evicted statement is
        `min(expiry_timestamp, current_time + purge_after_sec)`, so hashes
        close to their natural expiry are drained sooner.

crates:
  - name: sc-statement-store
    bump: patch
